    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 680801bdae65e2f5e466c0f81e82a2fb4e2cc3c5 -->\nReady for the maintainer to merge.\n\n**What looks good**\n- `write_plate_stl()` (crates/app/tests/box_pick.rs:188-194) now builds `camcraft-box-pick-<pid>-<n>` from a process-wide `AtomicUsize`, so every call owns its directory. No shared path remains and the `remove_dir_all` is gone; `temp_dir()` is the only env use left.\n- Test code only; `expect` stays inside a test helper. No dependency, process-file or snapshot change.\n- Body has `Changelog: none`, the issue reference and an honest \"not exercised\" note.\n\n**Local results (merged state, no conflicts; main trial merge not needed, PR is MERGEABLE)**\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test box_pick`, two runs: 7 passed, 0 failed each.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test box_pick -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking):** each call leaves its small temp directory behind, as before; fine for a test.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
